    "programmeDescription": "Philosophy at Tilburg University studies ethics, philosophical anthropology and psychology, political and social philosophy, and philosophy of science and knowledge. Historical and contemporary philosophical texts support argument, interpretation and independent research.",
    "comparisonExplanation": "The UCR options connect philosophical study with social and literary interpretation, normative questions about institutions, or empirical mind and language research. They address related questions through different disciplines, while leaving gaps in Tilburg’s dedicated history, epistemology, metaphysics and philosophical-methods sequence. Shared rows indicate partial relationships rather than course equivalence.",
